<description>
Paint the teal outline of the right triangle determined by the missing corner of the grey-marker square.

Input structure
The grid is an orange background with exactly four foreground marker pixels of one color. The markers have a square bounding box: three markers are bbox corners, and the fourth marker is inside that square.
Rule
Find the one corner of the marker bounding square that has no marker. That missing corner is the right-angle vertex of a right isosceles triangle; paint its two axis-aligned legs and the opposite diagonal in teal, leaving existing marker pixels unchanged.
Key insight
The present corner marker opposite the missing corner is a decoy; the three triangle vertices are the missing corner and the two marker corners adjacent to it.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "four grey marker pixels whose bbox is a square with exactly one missing corner",
  "transform": "paint teal on the outline of the right triangle inside the square: the missing bbox corner is the right-angle vertex, the two adjacent marker corners are the other vertices; keep grey markers unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8x8 [observed]
  background: orange (7)
  markers:
    color: grey (5) [observed]; any color except teal and background works per solver
    count: exactly 4
    bounding_box: square with side length 3-7
    layout: 3 of 4 bbox corners occupied; 4th marker is 1 diagonal step inward from the missing corner toward the opposite corner
    missing_corner: any of TL/TR/BL/BR (all four seen across examples)
  output:
    triangle_color: teal (8)
    triangle: right isosceles triangle inscribed in the marker bbox
    right_angle_vertex: the missing corner
    legs: two axis-aligned edges of the bbox adjacent to the missing corner
    hypotenuse: diagonal from one adjacent corner to the other
    rule: paint all outline pixels teal except where a grey marker already sits
    pixel_count: 3*(side+1) - 3 total outline pixels, minus 2 markers on outline = teal pixels

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (constraints are simple enough)
