    1. Choose grid size (8x8 observed, may vary 7-12 for diversity).
    2. Pick background color (orange observed) and marker color (grey observed); ensure neither is teal.
    3. Pick square side length S in [3, grid_size-1]. Pick top-left corner (r0,c0) so bbox fits in grid.
    4. Choose which corner to omit (TL/TR/BL/BR uniformly).
    5. Place markers at the 3 present bbox corners.
    6. Place 4th marker 1 diagonal step from missing corner toward opposite corner.
    7. Fill rest of grid with background. Verify exactly 4 non-bg pixels.
