<description>
Extend each non-background pixel into an L reaching the nearest vertical and horizontal grid edges.

Input structure
A mostly background grid contains one or more isolated foreground marker pixels.
Each marker is closer to one vertical edge and one horizontal edge, with no midpoint ties.

Rule
For every marker at (r, c), draw its color along column c from the marker to the nearer
top or bottom edge, and along row r from the marker to the nearer left or right edge.

Key insight
Each single pixel is the corner of an edge-facing L; its directions are chosen by nearest
grid-boundary distance rather than by color identity.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "isolated non-background marker pixels s",
  "path": "from each s, one straight ray along s.column to the nearer top/bottom grid edge and one straight ray along s.row to the nearer left/right grid edge",
  "trajectory": "paint every cell on both rays with s.color, including s",
  "transform": "keep all markers and combine the independently painted L shapes on the same canvas"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-16 rows x 8-16 cols, same size in/out, background 0
  markers:
    count: 1-4 isolated non-bg pixels
    colors: each marker has a distinct non-zero color
    isolation: all 8-neighbors of each marker must be bg
    position: no marker at row or column midpoint (r != (h-1)/2, c != (w-1)/2)
    quadrant: each marker occupies a unique quadrant (top/bottom x left/right) [observed]
    min_edge_dist: nearest-edge distance >= 1 on each axis
  transform: |
    For each marker at (r,c) with color C:
      - vertical ray: fill column c from r to the nearer top/bottom edge with C
      - horizontal ray: fill row r from r to the nearer left/right edge with C
      Result is an L-shape whose corner is the marker, pointing toward the nearest grid corner.
  non_overlap: L-shapes from different markers must not share any cell

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Pick grid dims h,w in [8,16]; avoid both-odd on same axis only if marker would land on midpoint (checked per-marker later)
    - Choose n_markers in [1,4]
    - For each marker, assign a unique quadrant from {TL,TR,BL,BR}; pick a distinct non-zero color
    - Place each marker at (r,c) in its quadrant, ensuring r != (h-1)/2, c != (w-1)/2, all 8-neighbors are bg, and the resulting L-shape (vertical+horizontal ray to nearest corner) does not overlap any previously placed L-shape
    - Build the output by painting all L-shapes
    - The input is just the grid with only the marker pixels (remove the rays)
```
